---
// The one chart on the site: measured CPU against the Free plan's 10 ms budget.
// Editorial dumbbells, not coloured status bars: a hairline is the measured spread,
// a hollow square is the floor, a solid square is the ceiling, and a hollow circle is
// a percentile. One accent — the native JS handler — is the only focal mark. Status is
// written in words next to each value; colour never has to carry it alone.
//
// Log scale, because the interesting numbers span four orders of magnitude — and a
// linear axis would draw the compiled handler as a zero-width line, which is a lie of
// a different kind. Every number is the source's own; the audit re-states each one.
const W = 920;
const H = 304;
const PAD_L = 128;
const PAD_R = 28;
const MIN = 1;
const MAX = 2600;
const x = (ms) => PAD_L + (Math.log10(ms) - Math.log10(MIN)) / (Math.log10(MAX) - Math.log10(MIN)) * (W - PAD_L - PAD_R);
const ticks = [1, 10, 100, 1000, 2000];

const rows = [
  {
    y: 96,
    label: 'php-in-worker',
    sub: 'cold boot',
    from: 1008,
    to: 2018,
    dots: [],
    value: '1,008–2,018 ms',
    tag: 'over budget',
    side: 'left',
  },
  {
    y: 176,
    label: 'kernel hot paths',
    sub: 'page-like probe',
    from: 5,
    to: 62,
    dots: [5, 41],
    value: 'p50 5 · p95 41 · max 62',
    tag: 'tail over',
  },
  {
    y: 256,
    label: 'port handler',
    sub: 'native JS',
    from: 1,
    to: 6,
    dots: [],
    value: '1–6 ms',
    tag: 'fits',
    focal: true,
  },
];
const budgetX = x(10);
---

<figure class="budgetfig">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-labelledby="budget-title budget-desc" class="budgetfig__svg">
    <title id="budget-title">Measured CPU per request against the Free plan's 10 ms budget</title>
    <desc id="budget-desc">
      On a logarithmic axis from 1 to 2,600 milliseconds: a PHP-in-Worker cold boot measured
      1,008 to 2,018 milliseconds; the kernel's page-like load measured a p50 of 5, a p95 of 41 and a
      max of 62 milliseconds; a hand-written port handler measured 1 to 6 milliseconds. The dashed
      line is the Free plan's 10 millisecond budget. Hollow squares mark the low end of each
      measured spread, solid squares the high end, hollow circles the p50 and p95. The native JS
      handler is the single accented mark.
    </desc>

    <g class="bf-grid">
      {ticks.map((ms) => (
        <g>
          <line x1={x(ms)} y1="64" x2={x(ms)} y2="280" />
          <text x={x(ms)} y="300" text-anchor="middle">{ms >= 1000 ? `${ms / 1000},000` : ms}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
    </g>

    <line class="bf-budget" x1={budgetX} y1="56" x2={budgetX} y2="280" />
    <text class="bf-budgetlabel" x={budgetX + 8} y="48">10 ms budget</text>

    {rows.map((row) => (
      <g class={`bf-row${row.focal ? ' bf-row--focal' : ''}`}>
        <text class="bf-label" x={PAD_L - 16} y={row.y - 4} text-anchor="end">{row.label}</text>
        <text class="bf-sub" x={PAD_L - 16} y={row.y + 16} text-anchor="end">{row.sub}</text>

        <line class="bf-span" x1={x(row.from)} y1={row.y} x2={x(row.to)} y2={row.y} />
        <rect class="bf-cap" x={x(row.from) - 4} y={row.y - 4} width="8" height="8" />
        <rect class={row.focal ? 'bf-cap bf-cap--focal' : 'bf-cap bf-cap--end'} x={x(row.to) - 4} y={row.y - 4} width="8" height="8" />
        {row.dots.map((dot) => (
          <circle class="bf-dot" cx={x(dot)} cy={row.y} r="3" />
        ))}

        <text
          class="bf-value"
          x={row.side === 'left' ? x(row.from) - 14 : x(row.to) + 12}
          y={row.y - 4}
          text-anchor={row.side === 'left' ? 'end' : 'start'}
        >{row.value}</text>
        <text
          class={row.focal ? 'bf-tag bf-tag--focal' : 'bf-tag'}
          x={row.side === 'left' ? x(row.from) - 14 : x(row.to) + 12}
          y={row.y + 16}
          text-anchor={row.side === 'left' ? 'end' : 'start'}
        >{row.tag}</text>
      </g>
    ))}
  </svg>

  <!-- Under 52rem the 920-unit chart would shrink its 9px labels below legibility. -->
  <ol class="budgetfig__mobile">
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <li>
        <span class="bf-m-label">{row.label}</span>
        <span class="bf-m-value">{row.sub} — {row.value} · {row.tag}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <figcaption>
    Log scale, 1 ms to 2,000 ms per request. A hairline is the spread the probe recorded; a hollow
    square is its low end, a solid square its high end, and a hollow circle a percentile. Sources:
    <span class="mono">MAP.md</span> §1 (the PHP-in-Worker probe), the project's
    <span class="mono">npm run gate:cpu</span> (page-like load, read back from the platform's own
    cpuTime and outcome) and the port-handler probe.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
